  "scope": "D298 exact complete-batch search-direction scheduling by cumulative scanned edge count instead of current queue size. Each nonstale popped row contributes its actual CSR degree; counter wrap changes only work ordering. Original band64,32-row batches, full distances/zero/MAX weights, stale checks, full64 fallbacks and conservative between-batch stopping remain. No answer cutoff, graph catalogue, seed/PGO/harness/host change. Conceptual inspiration from edge-balanced bidirectional search; this is NOT the paper exact edge-at-a-time algorithm or its instance-optimality theorem. Three full/public1/6/12 screen first; new independent all-pairs/zero/wide/skew/exhaustion/stopping/race/strict/GCC/image/default/actual proof before promotion.",
